 invariant is the thing to say out loud in the interview.\n\nO(n) time, O(1) extra space apart from the tiny digit string.\n\n**Common mistakes:** writing a count of `1` (the spec says omit it); writing the count as a single element `\"12\"` instead of two slots; building a new list and copying it back (works but violates the space requirement); mishandling the final run when the loop ends.\n\n**Interview follow-ups:** Decompress the result and discuss ambiguity when the input itself contains digits (a real RLE format needs an escape or a fixed-width count). What if the compressed form could be longer than the input (e.g. `\"abc\"` with counts always written)? Then in-place is impossible without first measuring the output length. Streaming compression: emit a run when the character changes, carrying only (char, count) state.","complexity":{"time":"O(n)","space":"O(1)"},"similar":["count-and-say","encode-and-decode-strings","remove-duplicates-from-sorted-array"],"number":193,"starter":"class Solution:\n    def compress(self, chars: List[str]) -> int:\n        pass\n"}